        "title": "Watchmaking - 01 Early Timekeeping",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every pre-mechanical timekeeping system reduces to one of three physical phenomena: the motion of celestial bodies (shadow casting, star positions), fluid flow (water, sand), or combustion (candle, incense). Each has a characteristic error source, and the engineering history of each is the story of compensating for that error."
